Some of the functions that turn js blobs into canvas objects are typed as
'any', which means that if I update an object's definition it is very easy to
introduce a bug.  I should add a more strictly typed version of this.


Update:
------
Gone are the anys and I also refactor all the unstripping code to use a single
function.  There's slightly more copies now, but I think there was some
undetected bugs around sharing state that I wasn't detecting. Although maybe
not, it was about sharing points arrays, but that only matters if it can be edited?
idk. I can easily add a flag to use the less-safe behavior or whatever.
